// THE PRESENTATION SEAM (A2, operator-directed 2026-08-01;
// docs/plans/roadmap-presentation-seam-design.md). One projection layer between the
// roadmap/workflow authorities and every renderer: the renderer receives an ALREADY-DECIDED
// presentation — no punctuation splitting, title reconstruction, policy on string content,
// availability-implies-emphasis, or evidence smuggled into an actuator region. Governing law: a
// stronger interface makes fewer claims, each at the right altitude, and shows the evidence or
// consequence that makes it matter; truthful atoms do not compose into a truthful presentation,
// so hierarchy, causality and relevance are modeled HERE, not improvised per renderer. Regions:
// Primary (what this work is), Activity (what is happening to it), Action (what the user can
// do), Evidence (why the activity claim is believed), Disclosure (complete detail).
// ActivityRegion is NOT a kind of ActuatorRegion — the A1-era fusion of process evidence into
// the actuator cell is the falsifier specimen this module dissolves. DELIBERATE ABSENCE: no
// progress_percent field, and none may be added — the seven obligations are independently
// evidenced facts, not percentage increments; a scalar appears only if the graph establishes one
// (making the false scalar UNWRITABLE is the §5 construction form of the rule).

// ONE projection authority across server and client (operator constraint 1, 2026-08-01). The
// dangerous shape is two: the server folding facts to HTML here while client TypeScript
// separately decides which segment is the summary, which evidence is routine, when an anomaly
// expands, or whether an action is prominent. Rule: every presentation DECISION lives in this
// module's pure fns; the dynamic endpoint serializes the DECIDED view fields (summary text,
// attention key, remaining count, evidence rows, action availability x priority) and the client
// PAINTS them without policy. Discharged by a parity witness — server-rendered activity state and
// the client-updated realization of the same facts yield the same semantic regions and labels —
// landing with the client-realization slice, not as prose.

// The attention axis drives expand/collapse (routine collapses, active work is legible, anomaly
// expands): Routine renders the one-line summary with the ledger behind disclosure; Anomalous
// auto-expands the located evidence — the row-level twin of gunbc.roadmap_altitude's section law.
// A NeedsUser arm was REMOVED (operator review 2026-08-01, minimality): no producer in the corpus
// yields a waiting-on-human fact yet, and an unconstructible attention state is future
// vocabulary — the arm returns WITH its producer.

type ActivityAttention
  = ActivityRoutine
  | ActivityAnomalous

type ActivityEvidenceRow {
  label: String
  value: String
}

// ActivityView is the decided answer to 'what is happening to this work', derived ONLY from
// evidence the workflow authorities already establish: a PROJECTION of WorkflowAttemptProgress
// (itself a pure fail-closed projection over WorkflowAttemptEvidence, per
// workflow_progress_projection_note), never a second progress authority. remaining_obligation_count
// projects from the reconcile report's fold result; obligation identity and order come from the
// canonical segment roster (roadmap_attempt_workflow_segment_kinds via the progress segments); the
// summary projects from the reconciled Agent segment state, which IS the provider-execution
// projection — nothing is recomputed here. NoActiveWork is the ROUTINE state and renders NOTHING:
// no hollow lamps, no seven pending chips; absence earns no row area. ActiveWork carries one
// consequence-first summary sentence ('Agent turn completed · Verification next', never a raw
// evidence pair the reader must join), the obligation ledger for disclosure, the derived remaining
// count, and the evidence rows grounding the summary (session container / worker process — stated
// as evidence, never as actions). ActiveWorkRefused carries the located reason: a refusal is a
// first-class state, not a styling variant of progress. CompletedWork is the terminal projection —
// the receipt-backed outcome, not the machinery. ActivityUnobservable is 'the evidence could not
// be read', distinct from refusal and absence — collapsing it into either is the state-space
// conflation §5 names. NAMING: the field is current_activity, not latest_observation — the event
// authority establishes no temporal order across observation channels, so 'latest' would claim an
// ordering nobody derived.

type ActivityView
  = NoActiveWork
  | ActiveWork {
      summary: String
      obligations: List<WorkflowSegment>
      remaining_obligation_count: Int
      current_activity: String
      attention: ActivityAttention
      evidence: List<ActivityEvidenceRow>
    }
  | ActiveWorkRefused {
      summary: String
      located_reason: String
      evidence: List<ActivityEvidenceRow>
    }
  | LegacySupersedableAttempt {
      summary: String
      located_reason: String
      attempt_key: String
      evidence: List<ActivityEvidenceRow>
    }
  | CompletedWork {
      outcome: String
      evidence: List<ActivityEvidenceRow>
    }
  | ActivityUnobservable {
      reason: String
    }

// The EXACT constructor over typed attempt facts (operator constraint 3, 2026-08-01): 'active'
// never means a string heuristic or a disjunction of narrower facts that can disagree (session
// present OR lamp on OR dispatch accepted OR process exists). The caller states which typed
// evidence situation holds; the refused and terminal arms are DERIVED from the progress facts, not
// caller-assertable — a fabricated refusal or completion is unwritable here.

type WorkAttemptFacts
  = NoActiveAttempt
  | ActiveAttempt { progress: WorkflowAttemptProgress }
  | AttemptUnobservable { reason: String }

// ActiveAttempt carries the progress projection ALONE (operator blocker 3, 2026-08-01): the first
// cut also took process and current_activity as parameters, making disagreement writable — a
// progress reconciled under WorkerProcessRunning beside an asserted WorkerProcessExited.
// WorkflowAttemptProgress already carries process (the shared worker_lifecycle evidence) and
// provider (whose provider_execution_activity IS the canonical current-activity projection), so
// the seam reads both from one carrier and the fork is unwritable.

// Availability and priority are ORTHOGONAL axes (the A1 recon's 'ten equally loud pills' defect):
// that an operation is legally available says nothing about how loudly it renders. Availability is
// a fact about the admission contract — for dispatch it is the projection of
// gunbc.roadmap_launch_admission, the same decision POST /dispatch and the belt tick consume
// (RLM-1), so the page can never claim a launch the route would refuse; priority is a presentation
// decision this seam owns. The renderer derives prominence from BOTH; availability never implies
// visual primacy. AvailableAsOverride is GONE: the manual out-of-order dispatch it named (a
// blocked, unsized, review or done row launchable by click) was a second launch authority beside
// the belt's, removed by the plan; any break-glass path is a separate type, endpoint,
// authorization and receipt, not an availability arm.

type ActionAvailability
  = ActionUnavailable
  | ActionAvailable

type ActionPriority
  = PrimaryAction
  | SecondaryAction
  | DiagnosticAction

type WorkActionKind
  = DispatchAction
  | ClearSessionAction

// An available dispatch action carries the LaunchIdentity the admission produced for this render
// (node, cause=operator, mode, instance, revision), so the page projects the same decision record
// the route and timer bind to their attempts. Rendered as evidence (data-launch-* attributes), NOT
// authorization: the button posts only the node id and the route re-observes the host and
// re-admits. Absent on every unavailable action.

type WorkAction {
  kind: WorkActionKind
  availability: ActionAvailability
  priority: ActionPriority
  label: String
  detail: String
  launch: LaunchIdentity?
}

type ActionView {
  primary_action: WorkAction?
  secondary_actions: List<WorkAction>
}

// In roadmap context, workflow means the work item's lifecycle; compiler and CI execution workflow
// stays under v2.workflow. The ruling names seven independent facts, each owned by its existing
// typed authority: Ready by gunbc.roadmap_spawner.node_is_spawnable; Live by
// gunbc.roadmap_dispatch_actuator.DispatchLiveSession keyed through the node-grain tmux session
// name; Attempted by dispatch_attempt_refs keyed through the attempt branch; Proposed and Landed by
// extdeps.github.pulls.PullRequest observations once the missing typed binding exists; Done by
// RoadmapNode.signoff; Superseded by SupersededLine.by. This note records the join ruling only —
// not an executable roster, not a re-declaration, never to be enumerated as workflow status data.
// The facts have no total order and several may hold at once (Live and Landed, Attempted and
// Superseded, Landed but not Done); a UI may order or group them for presentation only. Proposed
// and Landed stay blocked until one typed attempt-keyed carrier joins RoadmapNodeId, attempt key,
// branch, and PullRequest identity. (Re-homed from the deleted gunbc.client_observation_state
// module, whose four-state lamp vocabulary dissolved into ActivityView at A2; the class it guarded,
// unknowable-never-rounds-to-absent, is now carried by the ActivityUnobservable/NoActiveWork
// distinction and its executing witnesses.)

// Lifecycle and scheduling are DISTINCT axes the page previously fused into one status string:
// lifecycle is the node's own state (open/review/done/superseded; the node_status_symbol decision
// moved here as its single authority), scheduling is the frontier position (ready/upcoming/done/
// superseded buckets from spawn_frontier). A row can be lifecycle-open and scheduling-upcoming;
// collapsing them loses exactly the fact explaining why an open row is not dispatchable-now.

type WorkLifecycle
  = OpenLifecycle
  | ReviewLifecycle
  | DoneLifecycle
  | SupersededLifecycle

fn work_lifecycle(rn: RoadmapNode, merged: List<Int>) -> WorkLifecycle {
  if item_superseded_by(item: rn.line) == "" {
    if signoff_accepts(s: rn.signoff) {
      DoneLifecycle
    } else {
      if item_is_done(item: rn.line, merged: merged) { ReviewLifecycle } else { OpenLifecycle }
    }
  } else {
    SupersededLifecycle
  }
}

fn work_lifecycle_key(l: WorkLifecycle) -> String {
  match l {
    OpenLifecycle => "open"
    ReviewLifecycle => "review"
    DoneLifecycle => "done"
    SupersededLifecycle => "superseded"
  }
}

// Routine-state collapse (the A1 carried-forward miss; the altitude law's interface form — routine
// collapses, anomaly expands). OpenLifecycle is nearly every row's default, so an 'open' chip on
// each discriminates nothing and is permanent chrome; the DECIDED rule: the lifecycle chip renders
// only when the lifecycle departs the default (review/done/superseded). The state stays
// machine-readable: the row's node-<key> class and the altitude band counts consume
// work_lifecycle_key regardless, so collapsing the chip erases pixels, never the typed fact.
fn lifecycle_chip_renders(l: WorkLifecycle) -> Bool {
  match l {
    OpenLifecycle => false
    ReviewLifecycle => true
    DoneLifecycle => true
    SupersededLifecycle => true
  }
}

// The scheduling axis as a TYPED position, not a Bool (operator blocker 2, 2026-08-01: ready: Bool
// was anemic and caller-assertable — true could be passed for an upcoming node, and the view had no
// typed distinction among frontier positions). The arms project from the SAME predicates
// spawn_frontier filters — node_is_spawnable / node_is_upcoming / node_is_frontier_done /
// superseded — so scheduling equals frontier-bucket membership by construction (witnessed against
// spawn_frontier on the live authority, not asserted). SchedulingUpcoming carries its blockers, the
// unmet parents — why an open row is not dispatchable-now. SchedulingUnplanned is the honest arm
// for a node outside every bucket (unsized, or not yet admitted to the frontier); collapsing it
// into Upcoming would fabricate a blocked-on claim with no blockers.

type WorkScheduling
  = SchedulingReady
  | SchedulingUpcoming { blockers: List<String> }
  | SchedulingDone
  | SchedulingSuperseded
  | SchedulingUnplanned

fn scheduling_blockers(rn: RoadmapNode, nodes: List<RoadmapNode>, edges: List<RoadmapEdge>) -> List<String> {
  let parents = roadmap_parent_ids(edges: edges, node: rn.node)
  let unmet = filter(xs: parents, predicate: pid =>
    !any(nodes, n => n.node == pid && node_closes_dependency(n: n)))
  map(unmet, p => p as String)
}

fn work_scheduling(rn: RoadmapNode, nodes: List<RoadmapNode>, edges: List<RoadmapEdge>) -> WorkScheduling {
  if !(item_superseded_by(item: rn.line) == "") {
    SchedulingSuperseded
  } else {
    if node_is_frontier_done(n: rn) {
      SchedulingDone
    } else {
      if node_is_spawnable(n: rn, nodes: nodes, edges: edges) {
        SchedulingReady
      } else {
        if node_is_upcoming(n: rn, nodes: nodes, edges: edges) {
          SchedulingUpcoming { blockers: scheduling_blockers(rn: rn, nodes: nodes, edges: edges) }
        } else {
          SchedulingUnplanned
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

fn work_scheduling_key(s: WorkScheduling) -> String {
  match s {
    SchedulingReady => "ready"
    SchedulingUpcoming { blockers: _ } => "upcoming"
    SchedulingDone => "done"
    SchedulingSuperseded => "superseded"
    SchedulingUnplanned => "unplanned"
  }
}

// The quiet dependency line under the title, DECIDED here: it renders only for an Upcoming row with
// more than one blocker — a single parent is already told by the tree nesting, and a ready/done
// row's dependencies are met, so repeating them is noise re-dismissed on every row. (The A1
// renderer showed 'requires all' for any node with 2+ parents whatever its position; the seam
// narrows it to rows where the line answers 'why is this not dispatchable-now', the fact it exists
// to carry.)
fn scheduling_dependency_line(s: WorkScheduling) -> String? {
  match s {
    SchedulingUpcoming { blockers } =>
      if count(blockers) > 1 {
        Present { value: join(["requires all: ", join(blockers, ", ")], "") }
      } else {
        none
      }
    SchedulingReady => none
    SchedulingDone => none
    SchedulingSuperseded => none
    SchedulingUnplanned => none
  }
}

type SupportingFact {
  label: String
  value: String
  href: String
}

// WorkRowView is the decided row. headline comes from the ticket's own typed field — NEVER from
// recomposing '**headline** — brief' and re-splitting at punctuation (the round trip this seam
// deletes; legacy non-ticket lines keep the lead heuristic as a named residue INSIDE this
// projection only). summary is the row's one purpose-specific supporting claim (why-now /
// what-it-unlocks), Absent until an honest typed source exists — fabricating it by truncating the
// brief is prohibited (the explicit A1 re-scope). scheduling is the typed frontier position (its
// Upcoming arm CARRIES the blockers, so the quiet dependency line reads off the value the action
// derivation consumed — the first cut's separate blocked_on field was a dual representation and is
// gone). supporting_facts are demoted metadata (owner, sizing, carriers) rendered only under
// disclosure; disclosure is the decided full-detail region, serialized by the renderer without
// touching RoadmapItem.

// The disclosure region, decided: a ticket row projects its typed fields as labeled rows (the A1
// renderer's label vocabulary, now decided here so the renderer never reads TicketFields); a legacy
// line whose content is longer than its displayed lead projects the full content as the body; a
// row with neither has NoDisclosure and renders no details element beyond its supporting facts.
// Markdown-inline serialization of these strings is the renderer's job — serialization, not
// decision.
type DisclosureField {
  label: String
  value: String
}

type DisclosureNote {
  on: String
  note: String
}

type DisclosureView
  = NoDisclosure
  | TicketDisclosure {
      brief: String
      fields: List<DisclosureField>
      updates: List<DisclosureNote>
    }
  | LegacyBodyDisclosure { content: String }

type WorkRowView {
  node_id: String
  headline: String
  summary: String?
  lifecycle: WorkLifecycle
  scheduling: WorkScheduling
  superseded_by: String
  activity: ActivityView
  action: ActionView
  supporting_facts: List<SupportingFact>
  disclosure: DisclosureView
  rounds: HarnessRoundLedger
  worker_alive: Bool
}

fn intricacy_code(i: Intricacy) -> String {
  match i {
    IntricacyLow => "i:low"
    IntricacyMedium => "i:med"
    IntricacyHigh => "i:high"
  }
}

fn volume_code(v: Volume) -> String {
  match v {
    VolumeSmall => "v:small"
    VolumeMedium => "v:med"
    VolumeLarge => "v:large"
  }
}

fn sizing_fact(s: NodeSizing) -> List<SupportingFact> {
  match s {
    Unsized => []
    Sized { intricacy, volume, repo, acceptance } =>
      [ SupportingFact {
          label: "sizing",
          value: join([intricacy_code(i: intricacy), " ", volume_code(v: volume), " ", repo], ""),
          href: "",
        } ]
  }
}

fn owner_fact(owner: String) -> List<SupportingFact> {
  if owner == "" { [] } else { [ SupportingFact { label: "owner", value: join(["@", owner], ""), href: "" } ] }
}

fn carrier_facts(carriers: List<Pointer>) -> List<SupportingFact> {
  map(carriers, p => SupportingFact { label: "carrier", value: p.label, href: p.path })
}

fn row_supporting_facts(rn: RoadmapNode) -> List<SupportingFact> {
  concat(owner_fact(owner: rn.owner), concat(sizing_fact(s: rn.sizing), carrier_facts(carriers: rn.carriers)))
}

// The typed headline path: a TicketLine's headline IS ticket.headline — one field read, no markdown
// fusion, no delimiter recovery. Legacy variants (Derivable/Authored/Plain/Superseded) carry one
// content string and keep the lead-at-first-separator cut as this projection's named residue; when
// they gain typed headline fields the residue deletes here and nowhere else.
fn lead_before(full: String, delimiter: String) -> String? {
  let parts = split(s: full, delimiter: delimiter)
  if count(parts) > 1 {
    match parts.first() {
      Present { value: head } => Present { value: head }
      Absent => none
    }
  } else {
    none
  }
}

fn legacy_lead(full: String) -> String {
  match lead_before(full: full, delimiter: " — ") {
    Present { value: head } => head
    Absent =>
      match lead_before(full: full, delimiter: ". ") {
        Present { value: head } => head
        Absent => full
      }
  }
}

fn row_headline(line: RoadmapItem) -> String {
  match line {
    TicketLine { done: _, ticket } => ticket.headline
    DerivableLine { prs: _, title, description: _ } => legacy_lead(full: title)
    AuthoredLine { done: _, content } => legacy_lead(full: content)
    PlainLine { content } => legacy_lead(full: content)
    SupersededLine { by: _, content } => legacy_lead(full: content)
  }
}

fn row_summary(line: RoadmapItem) -> String? {
  none
}

fn disclosure_field(label: String, value: String) -> List<DisclosureField> {
  if value == "" { [] } else { [ DisclosureField { label: label, value: value } ] }
}

fn ticket_disclosure_fields(t: TicketFields) -> List<DisclosureField> {
  concat(disclosure_field(label: "displaced cost", value: t.displaced_cost),
    concat(disclosure_field(label: "current state", value: t.current_state),
      concat(disclosure_field(label: "first slice", value: t.first_slice),
        concat(disclosure_field(label: "red control", value: t.red_control),
          concat(disclosure_field(label: "out of scope", value: t.out_of_scope),
            concat(disclosure_field(label: "hand-back", value: t.handback),
              disclosure_field(label: "verified", value: join([t.authored_on, " · last verified ", t.last_verified_on], ""))))))))
}

fn row_disclosure(line: RoadmapItem) -> DisclosureView {
  match line_ticket(item: line) {
    Present { value: t } => TicketDisclosure {
      brief: t.brief,
      fields: ticket_disclosure_fields(t: t),
      updates: map(t.updates, u => DisclosureNote { on: u.on, note: u.note }),
    }
    Absent => {
      let full = match line {
        DerivableLine { prs: _, title, description: _ } => title
        AuthoredLine { done: _, content } => content
        PlainLine { content } => content
        SupersededLine { by: _, content } => content
        TicketLine { done: _, ticket } => ""
      }
      if full == row_headline(line: line) {
        NoDisclosure
      } else {
        LegacyBodyDisclosure { content: full }
      }
    }
  }
}

// The action derivation, both axes decided here. Dispatch availability is the LAUNCH ADMISSION'S
// verdict for cause Operator and nothing else (RLM-1): LaunchAdmitted renders ActionAvailable +
// PrimaryAction; LaunchRefused renders ActionUnavailable + SecondaryAction carrying the refusal's
// wire label and reason, so the row explains itself in the route's own words. Done and superseded
// lifecycles render no dispatch action (the remedy is acceptance history, not a launch). NO LONGER
// DERIVED: availability from the scheduling position — SchedulingReady used to be Available and
// every other open row AvailableAsOverride, re-deriving eligibility from the frontier in the page's
// words while the route derived it differently. NO LONGER FABRICATED (operator blocker 4,
// 2026-08-01): a ClearSessionAction; cleanup admission is an OBSERVED fact the sessions channel
// owns (session_action_view), and this fn derives dispatch alone.

type LaunchRowContext {
  standing: LaunchHostStanding
  graph: LaunchGraphStanding
  merged: List<Int>
}

fn row_launch_admission(ctx: LaunchRowContext, node_id: String) -> LaunchAdmission {
  launch_admission(
    cause: Operator,
    standing: ctx.standing,
    graph: ctx.graph,
    merged: ctx.merged,
    node_id: node_id,
    reserved: 0,
  )
}

fn dispatch_action(lifecycle: WorkLifecycle, admission: LaunchAdmission) -> List<WorkAction> {
  match lifecycle {
    DoneLifecycle => []
    SupersededLifecycle => []
    OpenLifecycle => [ dispatch_action_of_admission(admission: admission) ]
    ReviewLifecycle => [ dispatch_action_of_admission(admission: admission) ]
  }
}

fn dispatch_action_of_admission(admission: LaunchAdmission) -> WorkAction {
  match admission {
    LaunchAdmitted { identity } =>
      WorkAction {
        kind: DispatchAction,
        availability: ActionAvailable,
        priority: PrimaryAction,
        label: launch_admission_label(a: admission),
        detail: launch_admission_reason(a: admission),
        launch: Present { value: identity },
      }
    LaunchRefused { refusal: _ } =>
      WorkAction {
        kind: DispatchAction,
        availability: ActionUnavailable,
        priority: SecondaryAction,
        label: launch_admission_label(a: admission),
        detail: launch_admission_reason(a: admission),
        launch: none,
      }
  }
}

fn action_view(lifecycle: WorkLifecycle, admission: LaunchAdmission) -> ActionView {
  let dispatch = dispatch_action(lifecycle: lifecycle, admission: admission)
  let primary = fold(dispatch, init: none, f: (acc, a) => match a.priority {
    PrimaryAction => Present { value: a }
    SecondaryAction => acc
    DiagnosticAction => acc
  })
  let secondary = filter(xs: dispatch, predicate: a => match a.priority {
    PrimaryAction => false
    SecondaryAction => true
    DiagnosticAction => true
  })
  ActionView { primary_action: primary, secondary_actions: secondary }
}

// The summary sentence is consequence-first and derived from the reconcile facts, never hand-held
// per state: a refused/failed segment names itself with its located detail; an active Agent reads
// as working; a complete Agent with pending downstream obligations names the NEXT obligation and
// the remaining count (the ledger's fold result, not a recount). The session-present/process-exited
// pair projects as its consequence — 'the retained session is no longer running' — with the raw
// container/process facts demoted to evidence rows; the reader never joins tmux semantics manually.

fn first_non_complete(segments: List<WorkflowSegment>) -> WorkflowSegment? {
  fold(segments, init: none, f: (acc, s) => match acc {
    Present { value: v } => Present { value: v }
    Absent => match s.state {
      WorkflowSegmentComplete => none
      WorkflowSegmentStopped => none
      WorkflowSegmentPending => Present { value: s }
      WorkflowSegmentActive => Present { value: s }
      WorkflowSegmentFailed => Present { value: s }
      WorkflowSegmentRefused => Present { value: s }
    }
  })
}

fn first_refused(segments: List<WorkflowSegment>) -> WorkflowSegment? {
  fold(segments, init: none, f: (acc, s) => match acc {
    Present { value: v } => Present { value: v }
    Absent => match s.state {
      WorkflowSegmentRefused => Present { value: s }
      WorkflowSegmentFailed => none
      WorkflowSegmentComplete => none
      WorkflowSegmentStopped => none
      WorkflowSegmentPending => none
      WorkflowSegmentActive => none
    }
  })
}

fn first_failed(segments: List<WorkflowSegment>) -> WorkflowSegment? {
  fold(segments, init: none, f: (acc, s) => match acc {
    Present { value: v } => Present { value: v }
    Absent => match s.state {
      WorkflowSegmentFailed => Present { value: s }
      WorkflowSegmentRefused => none
      WorkflowSegmentComplete => none
      WorkflowSegmentStopped => none
      WorkflowSegmentPending => none
      WorkflowSegmentActive => none
    }
  })
}

fn segment_kind_is_agent(kind: WorkflowSegmentKind) -> Bool {
  match kind {
    EnvironmentWorkflowSegment => false
    WorkspaceWorkflowSegment => false
    AgentWorkflowSegment => true
    VerificationWorkflowSegment => false
    PublicationWorkflowSegment => false
    ReviewWorkflowSegment => false
    GoalAuditWorkflowSegment => false
  }
}

fn agent_segment_state(segments: List<WorkflowSegment>) -> WorkflowSegmentState {
  fold(segments, init: WorkflowSegmentPending, f: (acc, s) =>
    if segment_kind_is_agent(kind: s.kind) { s.state } else { acc })
}

// The operator's worked example: 'session container present' beside 'process exited' must never
// ship as an uninterpreted pair — the projection states the consequence and demotes the raw facts
// to evidence rows. The reconciliation contract (workflow_progress_projection_note) already makes
// Agent-complete imply a compatible process exit, but the seam derives the sentence from the
// process evidence rather than assuming the invariant, so contract drift reads as an odd sentence
// instead of a silent lie.

fn agent_completion_claim(process: WorkerProcessEvidence) -> String {
  match process {
    WorkerProcessExited { exit_code: _, last_command: _ } =>
      "Agent turn completed; the retained session is no longer running"
    WorkerProcessRunning { command: _ } => "Agent turn completed"
    WorkerProcessAbsent => "Agent turn completed; the worker session is gone"
    WorkerProcessUnobserved { reason: _ } =>
      "Agent turn completed; the worker process could not be observed"
  }
}

// Both evidence rows derive from the ONE process-evidence authority rather than a separate session
// Bool that could disagree with it: per belt_sessions_observation_separation_note, a running or
// exited pane implies a present session container, an unobserved pane probe maps a PRESENT session
// to process-unobserved, and Absent means no container was observed. A second session_present
// parameter would be the two-facts-one-truth fork §3 forbids.

fn session_container_value(process: WorkerProcessEvidence) -> String {
  match process {
    WorkerProcessRunning { command: _ } => "present"
    WorkerProcessExited { exit_code: _, last_command: _ } => "present"
    WorkerProcessUnobserved { reason: _ } => "present"
    WorkerProcessAbsent => "absent"
  }
}

// THROUGHPUT SITS BESIDE THE PROCESS ROW BECAUSE IT ANSWERS THE SAME QUESTION AT A DIFFERENT
// ALTITUDE. "worker process: running" says the attempt is alive; it cannot distinguish an agent
// producing tokens from one wedged on a backend that will never answer -- the state this deployment
// actually hit, where a POST stayed open past thirty minutes while the process stayed perfectly
// "running". A rate separates those two without the reader opening a transcript.
//
// AN UNMEASURED RATE RENDERS AS ITS REFUSAL, never as zero: throughput_cell_text carries the mark,
// so "no interval yet" and "measured slow" stay distinguishable in the cell itself.
fn activity_evidence_rows(
  process: WorkerProcessEvidence,
  throughput: HarnessThroughput,
) -> List<ActivityEvidenceRow> {
  [
    ActivityEvidenceRow {
      label: "session container",
      value: session_container_value(process: process),
    },
    ActivityEvidenceRow {
      label: "worker process",
      value: worker_process_evidence_label(evidence: process),
    },
    ActivityEvidenceRow {
      label: "throughput",
      value: throughput_cell_text(t: throughput),
    },
  ]
}

fn activity_summary(segments: List<WorkflowSegment>, remaining: Int, process: WorkerProcessEvidence) -> String {
  match agent_segment_state(segments: segments) {
    WorkflowSegmentActive => "Agent working"
    WorkflowSegmentComplete =>
      match first_non_complete(segments: segments) {
        Absent => "All obligations complete"
        Present { value: next } =>
          join([
            agent_completion_claim(process: process),
            " · ",
            workflow_segment_kind_label(kind: next.kind),
            " next · ",
            to_string(remaining),
            " remaining",
          ], "")
      }
    WorkflowSegmentStopped =>
      match first_non_complete(segments: segments) {
        Absent => "Agent stopped at its round budget · all obligations complete"
        Present { value: next } =>
          join([
            "Agent stopped at its round budget · ",
            workflow_segment_kind_label(kind: next.kind),
            " next · ",
            to_string(remaining),
            " remaining",
          ], "")
      }
    WorkflowSegmentPending => "Attempt admitted · agent not yet started"
    WorkflowSegmentFailed => "Agent run failed"
    WorkflowSegmentRefused => "Agent evidence refused"
  }
}

fn activity_view_from_parts(
  segments: List<WorkflowSegment>,
  remaining: Int,
  process: WorkerProcessEvidence,
  throughput: HarnessThroughput,
  current_activity: String,
) -> ActivityView {
  let evidence = activity_evidence_rows(process: process, throughput: throughput)
  match first_refused(segments: segments) {
    Present { value: refused } => ActiveWorkRefused {
      summary: join([workflow_segment_kind_label(kind: refused.kind), " evidence refused"], ""),
      located_reason: refused.detail,
      evidence: evidence,
    }
    Absent =>
      match first_failed(segments: segments) {
        Present { value: failed } => ActiveWork {
          summary: join([workflow_segment_kind_label(kind: failed.kind), " failed"], ""),
          obligations: segments,
          remaining_obligation_count: remaining,
          current_activity: current_activity,
          attention: ActivityAnomalous,
          evidence: evidence,
        }
        Absent =>
          match first_non_complete(segments: segments) {
            Absent => CompletedWork {
              outcome: "All obligations complete",
              evidence: evidence,
            }
            Present { value: _ } => ActiveWork {
              summary: activity_summary(segments: segments, remaining: remaining, process: process),
              obligations: segments,
              remaining_obligation_count: remaining,
              current_activity: current_activity,
              attention: ActivityRoutine,
              evidence: evidence,
            }
          }
      }
  }
}

fn activity_view_from_progress(progress: WorkflowAttemptProgress) -> ActivityView {
  match progress.provider {
    ProviderEventsRefused { activity, detail } =>
      if activity == legacy_attempt_supersedable_label {
        LegacySupersedableAttempt {
          summary: legacy_attempt_supersedable_label,
          located_reason: detail,
          attempt_key: attempt_key_short_form(key: progress.attempt_key),
          evidence: activity_evidence_rows(process: progress.process, throughput: harness_throughput_from_ledger(ledger: progress.rounds)),
        }
      } else {
        activity_view_from_parts(
          segments: progress.segments,
          remaining: progress.reconciliation.remaining_count,
          process: progress.process,
          throughput: harness_throughput_from_ledger(ledger: progress.rounds),
          current_activity: provider_execution_activity(state: progress.provider),
        )
      }
    _ =>
      activity_view_from_parts(
        segments: progress.segments,
        remaining: progress.reconciliation.remaining_count,
        process: progress.process,
        throughput: harness_throughput_from_ledger(ledger: progress.rounds),
        current_activity: provider_execution_activity(state: progress.provider),
      )
  }
}

fn activity_view_of(facts: WorkAttemptFacts) -> ActivityView {
  match facts {
    NoActiveAttempt => NoActiveWork
    AttemptUnobservable { reason } => ActivityUnobservable { reason: reason }
    ActiveAttempt { progress } => activity_view_from_progress(progress: progress)
  }
}

// THE ROUND LEDGER RIDES BESIDE THE ACTIVITY VIEW, NOT INSIDE IT. Both project from the same facts,
// but ActivityView answers "what is happening to this work" and is matched by name in dozens of
// arms; the ledger is the raw round-by-round record the strip paints from. Putting it on the view
// would make every consumer that matches a view arm name a field it never reads. Reading it off
// the same facts at the same seam keeps the fork unwritable -- there is one progress carrier and
// two projections of it -- without widening the view's contract.
fn rounds_of(facts: WorkAttemptFacts) -> HarnessRoundLedger {
  match facts {
    NoActiveAttempt => RoundsUnobserved { reason: "no active attempt" as NonEmptyStr }
    AttemptUnobservable { reason: _ } => RoundsUnobserved { reason: "attempt unobservable" as NonEmptyStr }
    ActiveAttempt { progress } => progress.rounds
  }
}


fn worker_alive_from_process(process: WorkerProcessEvidence) -> Bool {
  match process {
    WorkerProcessRunning { command: _ } => true
    WorkerProcessExited { exit_code: _, last_command: _ } => false
    WorkerProcessAbsent => false
    WorkerProcessUnobserved { reason: _ } => false
  }
}

fn work_row_view(
  rn: RoadmapNode,
  nodes: List<RoadmapNode>,
  edges: List<RoadmapEdge>,
  merged: List<Int>,
  activity: ActivityView,
  rounds: HarnessRoundLedger,
  launch: LaunchRowContext,
  worker_alive: Bool,
) -> WorkRowView {
  let lifecycle = work_lifecycle(rn: rn, merged: merged)
  let scheduling = work_scheduling(rn: rn, nodes: nodes, edges: edges)
  WorkRowView {
    node_id: rn.node as String,
    headline: row_headline(line: rn.line),
    summary: row_summary(line: rn.line),
    lifecycle: lifecycle,
    scheduling: scheduling,
    superseded_by: item_superseded_by(item: rn.line),
    activity: activity,
    action: action_view(lifecycle: lifecycle, admission: row_launch_admission(ctx: launch, node_id: rn.node as String)),
    supporting_facts: row_supporting_facts(rn: rn),
    disclosure: row_disclosure(line: rn.line),
    rounds: rounds,
    worker_alive: worker_alive,
  }
}

fn activity_attention_key(a: ActivityAttention) -> String {
  match a {
    ActivityRoutine => "routine"
    ActivityAnomalous => "anomalous"
  }
}

fn activity_arm_key(a: ActivityView) -> String {
  match a {
    NoActiveWork => "none"
    ActiveWork { summary: _, obligations: _, remaining_obligation_count: _, current_activity: _, attention: _, evidence: _ } => "active"
    ActiveWorkRefused { summary: _, located_reason: _, evidence: _ } => "refused"
    LegacySupersedableAttempt { summary: _, located_reason: _, attempt_key: _, evidence: _ } => "legacy_supersedable"
    CompletedWork { outcome: _, evidence: _ } => "completed"
    ActivityUnobservable { reason: _ } => "unobservable"
  }
}

// The composition constants BOTH realizations consume (the parity obligation's construction half):
// the server renderer joins obligation label/state/detail and evidence label/value with exactly
// these separators, and the emitted client embeds the same values as its string literals — one
// authority, so the realizations cannot drift on composition without the parity witness
// reddening. The disclosure summary word is here for the same reason: 'activity' must be the same
// word whether the details element was server-rendered or client-created.

data activity_state_sep: String = " · "
data activity_detail_sep: String = " — "
data activity_evidence_kv_sep: String = ": "
data activity_disclosure_label: String = "activity"

// The one visible line per arm, decided ONCE for both realizations: the server renderer and the
// emitted client compose the identical selection (active/refused → summary, completed → outcome,
// unobservable → the prefixed reason) — the parity witness holds them equal, so a drift in either
// realization reds rather than shipping two sentences for one state.

fn activity_summary_line(a: ActivityView) -> String {
  match a {
    NoActiveWork => ""
    ActiveWork { summary, obligations: _, remaining_obligation_count: _, current_activity: _, attention: _, evidence: _ } => summary
    ActiveWorkRefused { summary, located_reason: _, evidence: _ } => summary
    LegacySupersedableAttempt { summary, located_reason: _, attempt_key: _, evidence: _ } => summary
    CompletedWork { outcome, evidence: _ } => outcome
    ActivityUnobservable { reason } => join(["workflow evidence unobservable — ", reason], "")
  }
}

fn activity_evidence_row_json_value(row: ActivityEvidenceRow) -> JsonValue {
  json_object(members: [
    json_kv(key: "label", value: json_string(s: row.label)),
    json_kv(key: "value", value: json_string(s: row.value)),
  ])
}

// The wire realization of the DECIDED view — what makes the single projection authority real:
// /workflow.json carries these fields and the client paints them verbatim (arm selects the
// container's presence and material; summary/outcome/reason are final strings; attention is the
// expansion key; evidence rows are label/value pairs). The obligation ledger is NOT duplicated
// here — the attempt payload already carries the canonical segments and the client renders the
// ledger from those rows; a second segments copy under activity would be the dual representation
// §3 forbids.
fn activity_view_json_value(view: ActivityView) -> JsonValue {
  match view {
    NoActiveWork => json_object(members: [
      json_kv(key: "arm", value: json_string(s: "none")),
    ])
    ActiveWork { summary, obligations: _, remaining_obligation_count, current_activity, attention, evidence } =>
      json_object(members: [
        json_kv(key: "arm", value: json_string(s: "active")),
        json_kv(key: "summary", value: json_string(s: summary)),
        json_kv(key: "remaining_obligation_count", value: json_int(n: remaining_obligation_count)),
        json_kv(key: "current_activity", value: json_string(s: current_activity)),
        json_kv(key: "attention", value: json_string(s: activity_attention_key(a: attention))),
        json_kv(key: "evidence", value: json_array(elements: map(evidence, row => activity_evidence_row_json_value(row: row)))),
      ])
    ActiveWorkRefused { summary, located_reason, evidence } =>
      json_object(members: [
        json_kv(key: "arm", value: json_string(s: "refused")),
        json_kv(key: "summary", value: json_string(s: summary)),
        json_kv(key: "located_reason", value: json_string(s: located_reason)),
        json_kv(key: "evidence", value: json_array(elements: map(evidence, row => activity_evidence_row_json_value(row: row)))),
      ])
    LegacySupersedableAttempt { summary, located_reason, attempt_key, evidence } =>
      json_object(members: [
        json_kv(key: "arm", value: json_string(s: "legacy_supersedable")),
        json_kv(key: "summary", value: json_string(s: summary)),
        json_kv(key: "located_reason", value: json_string(s: located_reason)),
        json_kv(key: "attempt_key", value: json_string(s: attempt_key)),
        json_kv(key: "evidence", value: json_array(elements: map(evidence, row => activity_evidence_row_json_value(row: row)))),
      ])
    CompletedWork { outcome, evidence } =>
      json_object(members: [
        json_kv(key: "arm", value: json_string(s: "completed")),
        json_kv(key: "outcome", value: json_string(s: outcome)),
        json_kv(key: "evidence", value: json_array(elements: map(evidence, row => activity_evidence_row_json_value(row: row)))),
      ])
    ActivityUnobservable { reason } =>
      json_object(members: [
        json_kv(key: "arm", value: json_string(s: "unobservable")),
        json_kv(key: "reason", value: json_string(s: reason)),
      ])
  }
}

fn action_availability_key(a: ActionAvailability) -> String {
  match a {
    ActionUnavailable => "unavailable"
    ActionAvailable => "available"
  }
}

fn action_priority_key(p: ActionPriority) -> String {
  match p {
    PrimaryAction => "primary"
    SecondaryAction => "secondary"
    DiagnosticAction => "diagnostic"
  }
}

fn work_action_kind_key(k: WorkActionKind) -> String {
  match k {
    DispatchAction => "dispatch"
    ClearSessionAction => "clear-session"
  }
}

// The decided session-facts presentation (operator blocker 5, 2026-08-01). The prior client
// composed its own visible sentence — 'session · present — ' + process_state — and its own
// cleanup-button presentation from raw /sessions.json fields: a SECOND presentation authority
// beside this module for the same evidence. single_projection_authority_note applies to every
// channel: the sessions observer may update FACTS, it does not author display prose. This view
// decides the final visible line (presence is proven by wire inclusion, per
// belt_sessions_json_note), the title-channel detail, and the session action — whose availability
// comes from the OBSERVED cleanup admission (cleanup_allowed / cleanup_action / cleanup_detail),
// never inferred from activity state (blocker 4: an active attempt does not prove cleanup is
// allowed; ActionUnavailable is this arm's real consumer). The wire carries these decided fields
// under 'facts' and the client paints them verbatim.

type SessionActionView
  = NoSessionAction
  | SessionAction {
      kind: WorkActionKind
      availability: ActionAvailability
      priority: ActionPriority
      label: String
      detail: String
    }

type SessionFactsView {
  line: String
  detail: String
  action: SessionActionView
}

fn session_action_view(cleanup_action: String, cleanup_allowed: Bool, cleanup_detail: String) -> SessionActionView {
  if cleanup_action == "" {
    NoSessionAction
  } else {
    SessionAction {
      kind: ClearSessionAction,
      availability: if cleanup_allowed { ActionAvailable } else { ActionUnavailable },
      priority: DiagnosticAction,
      label: cleanup_action,
      detail: cleanup_detail,
    }
  }
}

fn session_facts_view(
  process: WorkerProcessEvidence,
  process_detail: String,
  provider: String,
  configured_provider: String,
  provider_readiness: String,
  session_name: String,
  cleanup_action: String,
  cleanup_allowed: Bool,
  cleanup_detail: String,
) -> SessionFactsView {
  SessionFactsView {
    line: join(["session · present — ", worker_process_evidence_label(evidence: process)], ""),
    detail: join([
      "provider ", provider,
      " (configured ", configured_provider,
      ", readiness ", provider_readiness, ") — ", session_name,
      if process_detail == "" { "" } else { join([" · ", process_detail], "") },
    ], ""),
    action: session_action_view(
      cleanup_action: cleanup_action,
      cleanup_allowed: cleanup_allowed,
      cleanup_detail: cleanup_detail,
    ),
  }
}

fn session_action_json_value(a: SessionActionView) -> JsonValue {
  match a {
    NoSessionAction => json_object(members: [
      json_kv(key: "kind", value: json_string(s: "none")),
    ])
    SessionAction { kind, availability, priority, label, detail } =>
      json_object(members: [
        json_kv(key: "kind", value: json_string(s: work_action_kind_key(k: kind))),
        json_kv(key: "availability", value: json_string(s: action_availability_key(a: availability))),
        json_kv(key: "priority", value: json_string(s: action_priority_key(p: priority))),
        json_kv(key: "label", value: json_string(s: label)),
        json_kv(key: "detail", value: json_string(s: detail)),
      ])
  }
}

fn session_facts_json_value(v: SessionFactsView) -> JsonValue {
  json_object(members: [
    json_kv(key: "line", value: json_string(s: v.line)),
    json_kv(key: "detail", value: json_string(s: v.detail)),
    json_kv(key: "action", value: session_action_json_value(a: v.action)),
  ])
}

// The local-denominator program claim plus its causal link to the work below (the A1 recon's item
// 5: without the relation the page is an inventory; with it, it begins to feel causal).
// ready_obligation_count counts the ready rows the focused program's lanes contribute — v0 states
// the relation for v1 exit as the focused program; a multi-program workspace generalizes the field
// to per-program rows.
type ProgramProgressView {
  name: String
  completed: Int
  total: Int
  ready_obligation_count: Int
}

// The composed workspace (operator blocker 6, 2026-08-01): active work surfaces ABOVE the ready
// queue — a row whose activity is ActiveWork or ActiveWorkRefused outranks any idle Ready row,
// whatever its frontier bucket. Remaining rows group by typed scheduling position. CompletedWork
// does NOT join the active band: all obligations complete is a receipt to read, not work in
// flight, so it stays in its scheduling bucket. program is the causal header claim
// (ProgramProgressView's consumer — the A1 compact strip re-grounds on this field).

// ONE failure narrated ONCE (operator blocker 6: the observation-refusal altitude split). When the
// workflow observation channel itself refuses, EVERY row's activity is unknowable from one cause —
// narrating it per row repeats one fact N times, per channel-banner AND per row N+1 times. Decided
// rule: the workspace carries one WorkspaceObservationImpact banner with the located reason, and a
// row whose activity is ActivityUnobservable is COVERED by it (workspace_covers_row_activity), so
// the renderer suppresses the per-row line — the row's typed state stays unobservable (never
// rounded to NoActiveWork; the row still carries the honest arm, so the fabrication is
// unwritable), only its NARRATION is deduplicated. A row-specific unobservable reason under a
// nominal workspace observation still narrates on its own row.

type ObservationImpactView
  = ObservationsNominal
  | WorkspaceObservationImpact {
      summary: String
      located_reason: String
    }

fn observation_impact_view(workflow_refused: String?) -> ObservationImpactView {
  match workflow_refused {
    Absent => ObservationsNominal
    Present { value: reason } => WorkspaceObservationImpact {
      summary: "workflow observation unavailable",
      located_reason: reason,
    }
  }
}

fn workspace_covers_row_activity(observation: ObservationImpactView, a: ActivityView) -> Bool {
  match observation {
    ObservationsNominal => false
    WorkspaceObservationImpact { summary: _, located_reason: _ } =>
      match a {
        ActivityUnobservable { reason: _ } => true
        NoActiveWork => false
        ActiveWork { summary: _, obligations: _, remaining_obligation_count: _, current_activity: _, attention: _, evidence: _ } => false
        ActiveWorkRefused { summary: _, located_reason: _, evidence: _ } => false
        LegacySupersedableAttempt { summary: _, located_reason: _, attempt_key: _, evidence: _ } => false
        CompletedWork { outcome: _, evidence: _ } => false
      }
  }
}

// Family-once grouping (the A1 carried-forward miss, staged behind the A2 core seam per the design
// note's witness item 9). A work family is a set of rows generated from ONE authority fn whose
// shared claim would otherwise repeat per row — the specimen is the closing-contract task
// generator, whose 'Write the closing check for: X' headline repeated the family claim N times on
// the daily page. Decided rule: the family claim is stated ONCE as the group header; each member
// row carries only its DISCRIMINATING SUBJECT — a typed field supplied by the generator that minted
// the member (the gated node's own ticket headline), NEVER recovered by parsing or prefix-stripping
// the fused headline (exactly the heuristic class this seam exists to kill; the no-parsing witness
// plants a subject containing the claim prose and an unlisted lookalike row to prove both
// directions). Membership is typed facts (WorkFamilyMemberFact rows derived from the generator's
// own pairs), so an unlisted row whose headline HAPPENS to start with the claim stays ungrouped. An
// active member leaves its group for the Active band — attention outranks taxonomy — and the group
// renders only its band's members at the position of its first member, preserving row order.

type WorkFamilyDecl {
  id: String
  claim: String
}

type WorkFamilyMemberFact {
  family_id: String
  task_node: String
  subject: String
}

type WorkFamilyView {
  id: String
  claim: String
  rows: List<WorkRowView>
}

type WorkBandEntry
  = BandRow { row: WorkRowView }
  | BandFamily { family: WorkFamilyView }

type DailyWorkspaceView {
  program: ProgramProgressView?
  observation: ObservationImpactView
  active: List<WorkRowView>
  ready: List<WorkBandEntry>
  upcoming: List<WorkBandEntry>
  done: List<WorkBandEntry>
  superseded: List<WorkBandEntry>
}

fn row_is_active_work(row: WorkRowView) -> Bool {
  match row.activity {
    ActiveWork { summary: _, obligations: _, remaining_obligation_count: _, current_activity: _, attention: _, evidence: _ } => true
    ActiveWorkRefused { summary: _, located_reason: _, evidence: _ } => true
    LegacySupersedableAttempt { summary: _, located_reason: _, attempt_key: _, evidence: _ } => true
    NoActiveWork => false
    CompletedWork { outcome: _, evidence: _ } => false
    ActivityUnobservable { reason: _ } => false
  }
}

fn rows_with_scheduling_key(rows: List<WorkRowView>, key: String) -> List<WorkRowView> {
  filter(xs: rows, predicate: r => !row_is_active_work(row: r) && work_scheduling_key(s: r.scheduling) == key)
}

fn family_member_for(members: List<WorkFamilyMemberFact>, node_id: String) -> WorkFamilyMemberFact? {
  fold(members, init: none, f: (acc, m) => match acc {
    Present { value: v } => Present { value: v }
    Absent => if m.task_node == node_id { Present { value: m } } else { none }
  })
}

fn family_subject_row(row: WorkRowView, subject: String) -> WorkRowView {
  WorkRowView {
    node_id: row.node_id,
    headline: subject,
    summary: row.summary,
    lifecycle: row.lifecycle,
    scheduling: row.scheduling,
    superseded_by: row.superseded_by,
    activity: row.activity,
    action: row.action,
    supporting_facts: row.supporting_facts,
    disclosure: row.disclosure,
    rounds: row.rounds,
    worker_alive: row.worker_alive,
  }
}

fn family_band_rows(rows: List<WorkRowView>, members: List<WorkFamilyMemberFact>, family_id: String) -> List<WorkRowView> {
  fold(rows, init: [], f: (acc, r) => match family_member_for(members: members, node_id: r.node_id) {
    Present { value: m } =>
      if m.family_id == family_id { append(acc, items: [family_subject_row(row: r, subject: m.subject)]) } else { acc }
    Absent => acc
  })
}

fn band_entries(
  rows: List<WorkRowView>,
  families: List<WorkFamilyDecl>,
  members: List<WorkFamilyMemberFact>,
) -> List<WorkBandEntry> {
  let grouped = fold(rows, init: BandEntriesAcc { entries: [], emitted_family_ids: [] }, f: (acc, r) =>
    match family_member_for(members: members, node_id: r.node_id) {
      Absent => BandEntriesAcc {
        entries: append(acc.entries, items: [BandRow { row: r }]),
        emitted_family_ids: acc.emitted_family_ids,
      }
      Present { value: m } =>
        if acc.emitted_family_ids |> any(fid => fid == m.family_id) {
          acc
        } else {
          match family_decl_for(families: families, family_id: m.family_id) {
            Present { value: decl } => BandEntriesAcc {
              entries: append(acc.entries, items: [BandFamily { family: WorkFamilyView {
                id: decl.id,
                claim: decl.claim,
                rows: family_band_rows(rows: rows, members: members, family_id: m.family_id),
              } }]),
              emitted_family_ids: append(acc.emitted_family_ids, items: [m.family_id]),
            }
            Absent => BandEntriesAcc {
              entries: append(acc.entries, items: [BandRow { row: r }]),
              emitted_family_ids: acc.emitted_family_ids,
            }
          }
        }
    })
  grouped.entries
}

type BandEntriesAcc {
  entries: List<WorkBandEntry>
  emitted_family_ids: List<String>
}

fn family_decl_for(families: List<WorkFamilyDecl>, family_id: String) -> WorkFamilyDecl? {
  fold(families, init: none, f: (acc, d) => match acc {
    Present { value: v } => Present { value: v }
    Absent => if d.id == family_id { Present { value: d } } else { none }
  })
}

fn daily_workspace_view(
  rows: List<WorkRowView>,
  program: ProgramProgressView?,
  observation: ObservationImpactView,
  families: List<WorkFamilyDecl>,
  members: List<WorkFamilyMemberFact>,
) -> DailyWorkspaceView {
  DailyWorkspaceView {
    program: program,
    observation: observation,
    active: filter(xs: rows, predicate: r => row_is_active_work(row: r)),
    ready: band_entries(rows: rows_with_scheduling_key(rows: rows, key: "ready"), families: families, members: members),
    upcoming: band_entries(rows: rows_with_scheduling_key(rows: rows, key: "upcoming"), families: families, members: members),
    done: band_entries(rows: rows_with_scheduling_key(rows: rows, key: "done"), families: families, members: members),
    superseded: band_entries(rows: rows_with_scheduling_key(rows: rows, key: "superseded"), families: families, members: members),
  }
}
